ChromatiX licensing
=======================

ChromatiX: the ModRetro Chromatic FPGA design rebuilt with LiteX.

ChromatiX is dual-licensed, per file (see the SPDX-License-Identifier of each file):

- Work derived from ModRetro's oss-chromatic-console-fpga (GPL-3.0): GPL-3.0-only
  (LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt). This covers the LiteX/Migen ports of the original design
  (chromatix.py and the gateware modules marked "Derived from ModRetro's
  oss-chromatic-console-fpga"), the register data extracted from it (chromatix/data/)
  and the Game Boy emulation wrapper (chromatix/verilog/emu/, see its LICENSE).

- Our own work (LiteX adaptation, new modules, tools, simulation, tests, documentation):
  BSD-2-Clause (LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt), copyright (C) 2026 Enjoy-Digital &
  ChromatiX developers.

Other authors retain ownership of their contributions. Contributions to BSD-2-Clause files are
expected under the BSD-2-Clause license, contributions to GPL-3.0-only files under the GPL-3.0.

Third-party components (under their own licenses):

- chromatix/verilog/emu/: includes files of the MiSTer Game Boy core (GPL-2.0+/GPL-3.0+,
  see file headers) and the SameBoy CGB boot ROM (MIT, Lior Halphon).
- chromatix/verilog/Gameboy_MiSTer/ (git submodule): MiSTer Game Boy core (GPL, see its
  sources).
- firmware/esp32-sdr/: builds ESP-SDR (GPL-3.0, fetched at build time, not included) with a
  Chromatic transport; esp-sdr-chromatic.patch is a patch of ESP-SDR (GPL-3.0), the resulting ESP32
  firmware is GPL-3.0.
- Python dependencies (not included): LiteX (BSD-2-Clause), Migen (BSD-2-Clause),
  Amaranth (BSD-2-Clause), LUNA (BSD-3-Clause).

Bitstreams built from this repository include GPL parts: they must be distributed under the
terms of the GPL.
